    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d890">

                <pb facs="0877" n="765" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg765"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conference 184.01602/73:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Admiral Bristol to the Commission to Negotiate
                        Peace</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-06-30T18:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 30, 1919—6
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received in Paris July 10, 1:30
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>971. [From Berry at Ekaterinodar:]</p>
                <p>Reference your undated telegram mailed in Constantinople June 12 and received
                    here June 25,<anchor n="16" xml:id="d890-f1"/> can state that no Russian
                    repatriates from France mutinied at Novorossisk or were exterminated. See Berry
                        22<anchor n="17" xml:id="d890-f2"/> for account of Russian detachment of 600
                    troops from French west front sent into line about May 13 and immediately
                    attempted to desert to Bolsheviki <hi rendition="#italic">en masse</hi> but
                    Volunteer commander had been forewarned and concealed machine guns finished most
                    of them. Presume this to be incident misunderstood in Paris. Kolchak
                        acceptance<anchor n="18" xml:id="d890-f3"/> of Allied note generally
                    applauded in /south Russia but text of note criticised on score of several
                    paragraphs dealing with future interior affairs which no person not even Kolchak
                    can truly give assurances at present time while major part of Russia is yet in
                    enemy’s hands. The paragraph suggesting survival of National Assembly severely
                    criticised and regarded as evidence of lack of knowledge of Russian affairs in
                    Paris as that assembly was established under Bolsheviki regime by Bolsheviki.
                    Berry.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bristol</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
